Fluid services connect machines, materials, energy and people (@fd-fluid-service: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/Elementary-Fluid-Dynamics-McDonough.lingua#r_7F9FTDV2VV4P28PG16J5PJSK18", #source "../sources/Water-Hammer-Ghidaoui-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_60QC37FY494KQ6Z6YEWDCCFYTN", #source "../sources/Fundamentals-of-Multiphase-Flow-Brennen.lingua#r_0T6RH2YC70Z23SR3H4QZDJ69JM", #fluid-dynamics "Keep-a-fluid-system-understood-through-change-and-maintenance.lingua#r_0VA875G7B5W9ZKP27DG3ZGPXTY") { r_14C278NFN0ZBZ903RME1NGZGBS
**Read:** [Lectures in Elementary Fluid Dynamics — James M. McDonough](../sources/Elementary-Fluid-Dynamics-McDonough.lingua#r_7F9FTDV2VV4P28PG16J5PJSK18), engineering applications and balances; [A Review of Water Hammer Theory and Practice — Ghidaoui and colleagues](../sources/Water-Hammer-Ghidaoui-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_60QC37FY494KQ6Z6YEWDCCFYTN), transient consequences for services; [Fundamentals of Multiphase Flow — Christopher E. Brennen](../sources/Fundamentals-of-Multiphase-Flow-Brennen.lingua#r_0T6RH2YC70Z23SR3H4QZDJ69JM), material-dependent transport limits.

Trace a service such as cooling-water circulation, clean gas delivery, ventilation, slurry transport or a process-liquid supply from its source to its users and return/disposal path. Specify the delivered quantity, quality, pressure, temperature and availability that the user actually needs. A pipe network is only part of that service.

Connect the fluid balance to pumps or compressors, power, treatment, thermal exchange, storage, controls, instrumentation, isolation, materials, maintenance and operating knowledge. Identify upstream/downstream dependencies and measurements that reveal deteriorating performance. Distinguish delivered flow from gross circulated flow, and account for leakage, recirculation and losses on the same basis.

Use the developed chemistry, metrology, thermal and power Records where a specific concept is needed, then pursue the full specialist subject for its unique knowledge. Explain how an ordinary pressure or flow observation can support a decision without pretending to identify every failure mechanism. The integration should remain a connected technical account with explicit handoffs among people and equipment.

**Continue:** [Keep a fluid system understood through change and maintenance](Keep-a-fluid-system-understood-through-change-and-maintenance.lingua#r_0VA875G7B5W9ZKP27DG3ZGPXTY).

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics — motion, forces, transport and evidence](../Fluid-dynamics.lingua#r_7PQW1WDHK708BFV23MD8ET61VZ).
